EXT. SCHOOL BUS STOP - BACK OF A DRIVE-IN THEATER - NIGHT

A cracked screen looms behind them. Moths circle a lone streetlight.

ZUZU, fifteen, grips a stolen bottle of cider. HOBART, fifteen, holds a flashlight. LINDIWE, sixteen, perches on a car hood. PABLO, fourteen, hugs his knees. MARGUERITE, sixteen, in a prom dress, shivers.

ZUZU
Hobart, put the light out.

HOBART
Marguerite's cold.

MARGUERITE
I'm fine. Lindiwe, give me your jacket.

LINDIWE
Pablo, share yours.

PABLO
It's a hoodie. It's too small.

ZUZU
Everybody shut up. Headlights.

A car passes on the road. Slows. Speeds up. They breathe.

PABLO
(whispering)
Was it my dad?

LINDIWE
No, Pablo. Your dad drives a Buick.

Marguerite starts laughing. Then Zuzu. Then all of them, helplessly, until Hobart drops the flashlight and it rolls under the car.
